    "note": "**M1b.1 — AUTO camera zoom (legibility-driven).** Per your rule, zoom is no longer fixed. The camera now asks *\"can every tile paint its number + dims legibly at the current viewport?\"* — if yes, **no zoom** (fit-to-panel); if not, it zooms the **minimum** needed so the smallest tile is legible, then pans to follow the walk.\n\nThis 2×2 layout → **no zoom** (what you wanted): all four tiles stay full-size and labeled. Zoom only engages as tiles get small:\n\n| layout | tiles | camera |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2×2 / 4×4 | 4–16 | **no zoom** |\n| 6×6 | 36 | zoom 1.37 |\n| 8×8 | 64 | zoom 1.83 |\n| 12×12 | 144 | zoom 2.75 |\n| 20×20 | 400 | zoom 4.0 (cap) |\n\nThe `cameraZoom` prop is now an **override** (omit = auto; `1` = force fit-to-panel; `>1` = force a zoom).",
    "question": "Confirm the 2×2 reads right with **no zoom** now. To see auto-zoom + follow engage, render a dense layout — e.g. `M0String` = an 8×8 grid (one-liner in chat). Is the legibility threshold about right, or should tiles be allowed smaller / forced bigger before zoom kicks in? If good, I'll start the **inspector panel (M2)**.",
